@title Online ticketing platform architecture
@subtitle Tidewater Ferries on Azure, region North Europe
@author Digital Channels
@date 2026-09-22

## Overview

Passengers book through Azure Front Door. Every booking is written to one database and announced as an event so that the scanners at the terminals stay in step.

## Diagram

diagram tix dir=TB title="Ticketing platform"
tix: pax "Passengers" user
tix: fd "Front Door" lb
tix: pay "Payment Provider" ext
tix: scan "Port Terminal Scanners" ext
tix: web "Booking Web App" svc focus
tix: api "Ticketing API" svc focus
tix: db "Reservations DB" db "Azure SQL"
tix: ev "Booking Events" queue "Service Bus"
tix: pax -> fd : HTTPS
tix: fd -> web : origin request
tix: web -> api : REST
tix: api -> db : SQL, port 1433
tix: api -> pay : card authorization
tix: api -> ev : ticket issued
tix: ev -> scan : sync every 30 s
tix: group app "App subnet 10.50.1.0/24" web, api
tix: group data "Data subnet 10.50.2.0/24" db, ev
tix: group vnet "Ticketing VNet 10.50.0.0/16" app, data
tix: group sub "Ticketing subscription" vnet

## Capacity

table = component,capacity; Booking Web App,3 to 10 instances at 60% CPU; Ticketing API,4 to 16 pods; Reservations DB,8 vCores with a read replica in the paired region

## Recovery targets

kpi Recovery point objective | 5 minutes
kpi Recovery time objective | 1 hour
kpi Last tested | 2026-08-19
